# Fleet choices about the mission itself, and the approach mystery thread.
# Arc and plants: content/STORY_BIBLE.md (spoilers). Voice: content/STYLE.md.

card dec_halfway
type decision
cat mission
days 24 24
weight 40
once
duration 1
roles A B
lean warm feast quiet
text Halfway, by the flight plan's clock. {A} wants to break out the good rations and mark it properly. {B} would rather not count yet.
option feast | Mark it | The fleet eats the good rations on eight screens at once. {A}'s toast to halfway turns into a toast to the people who packed the food.
  res food -2
  morale A 4
  morale B 2
option quiet | Let it pass | Halfway passes without a word on the fleet channel. On every ship, at the same minute, someone looks at the clock anyway.
  bond A B 3

card dec_name
type decision
cat mission
days 26 34
weight 10
once
duration 2
roles A B
lean curious after home
text The backup-site maps, stitched from imagery older than the cargo landings (the sharpest camera at Mars rode on the grey relay), show an unnamed crater small enough for the fleet to name. {A} wants to name it after the first person who ever wrote a Mars mission plan. {B} wants somewhere at home.
option after | Honor the planners | The name goes in the request. Somewhere, a committee will argue about it for years, which {A} considers part of the honor.
  set name_plan
  trait A curious 2
option home | Name it for home | The crater gets the name of a small town on Earth that most of Earth has never heard of. The town's paper runs it on the front page.
  set name_home
  trait B warm 3
  morale B 4

card dec_science
type decision
cat mission
days 18 23
weight 8
once
duration 2
roles A B
lean curious record save
text A gamma-ray burst goes off far past the galaxy, and every ship's X-ray monitor catches it. Timed against detectors near Earth, the raw buffers could pin the source, but pulling them home bumps a day of mail. {A} wants the data sent. {B} wants the letters.
option record | Send the data | The burst's source shrinks from a smear of sky to a thin arc, and the arc runs through one faint galaxy. {A} saves the confirmation in the photo folder.
  morale B -2
  trait A curious 3
  morale A 3
option save | Letters first | Ground telescopes get it anyway, less sharply. {B} reads every letter, and doesn't pretend it was an easy trade.
  trait B warm 2

# --- The mystery chain (fixed days; one beat a day from 35 to 41) ------------------
card m_ripple
type event
cat mystery
clue
days 14 14
weight 14
due
once
roles A
when cond A ok
text {A} cleans up the receiver's noise floor for the weekly report and finds a faint ripple in it, at about nine hundredths of a hertz. A control loop hunting somewhere, most likely the coolant pump's: it's on the same bus. "Pump's hunting," {A} tells the ground, and books it a service slot.

card m_dropout
type event
cat mystery
clue core
due
once
days 24 27
roles A
when since t_theory >= 2
text {A} plots a week of the old-channel carrier. It isn't steady: there for part of each day, gone for the rest, and back a little later each morning than the last. It goes in the anomaly file, behind the dust forecast that's due first.

card m_theory
type event
cat mystery
due
once
days 17 18
roles A
when since t_carrier >= 2
when !is A ow_list
when !is A ow_song
when !is A ow_garden
when !is A ow_letter
when !is A ow_dose
when !is A ow_hail
text {A} looks up the grey relay. Its thruster stuck open before the cargo landings; in its last week on the books, three power-only passes caught a pulse every 10.96 seconds, 2.4 percent of the time; the ground read it as a spin. Nothing else used the channel. {A} sketches a lighthouse in blue.
do who ow_theory A
do mark t_theory
do morale A 3

card m_theory_confirm
type event
cat mystery
clue
due
once
days 25 27
roles A
when since t_theory >= 3
when is A ow_theory
text The ground can't run the grey relay forward: its orbit data is two years stale. The ground sends the last good ephemeris anyway, and an apology. {A} slides the lighthouse sketch into the flight-plan binder.
do morale A 2

card c_theory
type beat
cat human
due
once
days 38 38
roles A
when is A ow_theory
text {A} looks at the lighthouse again. Timed to the microsecond, every knock runs a hundredth of a second early, then late, once a day, and the day is thirty-seven minutes too long. {A} writes "24 h 37 m" under the lighthouse and says nothing at all.
do trait A curious 2

card m_flash1
type event
cat mystery
clue core
due
once
days 30 31
roles A
when !is A ow_theory
when !is A ow_hail
text {A} pulls an old survey orbiter's low-light night frames of the landing region. On dark ground near the edge of one frame, one pixel is lit. On the next frame it isn't. A cosmic-ray hit on the sensor, like the hundred before it. {A} plots it anyway.
do set flash_seen
do mark t_flash
do who flash_who A
do trait A curious 2

card m_flash2
type event
cat mystery
due
once
days 32 33
roles A
when flag flash_seen
when since t_flash >= 2
when is A flash_who
text {A} goes through every night frame of that patch this month. Every pass, on different rows of the sensor, the lit pixel lands on the same spot of ground. {A} sends the list round. The ground checks its list: nearest on file is the hopper, tipped on its pad, beacon still coming and going.
do set flash_twice
do open dec_flash

card dec_flash
type decision
cat mystery
days 32 33
weight 1
once
duration 1
roles A B
when flag flash_twice
lean curious look leave
text {A} wants to ask the ground to task an orbiter for a fast sequence over the lit pixel, at the cost of the fleet's next deep-space pass: every letter from home waits. {B} would leave it for the people who'll be down there with time to look.
option look | Ask for the sequence | The request goes up. {A} writes the apology to seven inboxes personally, and means each one.
  set flash_looked
  morale A -2
  morale B -2
option leave | Leave it for the ground | The pixel goes into the anomaly file, under a heading {B} writes in capitals. The letters from home arrive on time, all of them.
  set flash_left
  morale B 2

card m_key
type event
cat mystery
clue core key
due
once
days 34 34
roles A
text The ground decodes a whole frame: a link request on an old key, sequence 5,750,112, with a fresh challenge; the next frame brings a new one, and the next. {A} does the sum: two years at least. The ground: "Old key. Only the relay, the write-offs and our fallback kept it. None of it is on the books."
do trait A curious 2

card flash_answer
type event
cat mystery
clue core ground
due
once
days 35 36
roles A
when flag flash_looked
when since t_flash >= 5
when is A flash_who
text The fast sequence comes down overnight: forty frames of dark ground as the orbiter slides over. The pixel lights, goes out, lights again, and never moves against the rocks. {A} counts the frames between flashes, gets the same number each time, and calls the fleet.
do set flash_ground
do trait A curious 4

card flash_answer_ground
type event
cat mystery
clue core ground
due
once
days 35 36
roles A
when flag flash_left
when since t_flash >= 5
when is A flash_who
text An email from the orbiter team reaches {A}: a calibration slot was free, and the pixel was in the swath. Dark ground, the pixel lighting, going out, lighting again, never moving against the rocks. Forty frames.
do set flash_ground
do trait A curious 3

card c2_cold
type event
cat grim
due
once
days 36 37
roles A
when is A flash_who
when !fired h_band
text The night frames of the pixel have gaps now, longest in the hour before dawn, the coldest there. Each night a gap runs a few knocks longer, and it comes back on the beat. {A} plots the gaps against the calendar: at this rate they meet in the middle a week or two after the fleet lands.
do morale A -2

card m_overlay
type event
cat mystery
clue core
due
once
days 36 37
roles A
when flag flash_ground
when !is A ow_hail
when !is A flash_who
when !is A ow_theory
text {A} borrows the old-channel receiver record, slides it back by the one-way light time from Mars, just under half a minute, and lays it over the forty frames. The carrier peaks on the exact frame the pixel lights. Every time. {A} puts both traces on the galley screen, side by side.
do trait A curious 3

card m_checked
type event
cat mystery
due
once
days 37 38
roles A
when fired m_overlay
when flag flash_looked
text The ground answers the overlay: nothing on file near that pixel should have power. Nearest is still the hopper, if it bounced when it tipped; its last fix is two years old and good to ninety kilometres. Two weeks of hails on the old key, unanswered. On the list it goes.
do morale A 1

card m_checked_g
type event
cat mystery
due
once
days 37 38
roles A
when fired m_overlay
when flag flash_left
text The ground answers the overlay: nothing on file near that pixel should have power. Nearest is still the hopper, if it bounced when it tipped; its last fix is two years old and good to ninety kilometres. Two weeks of hails on the old key, unanswered. "Surveying it."
do morale A 1

card m_listen
type event
cat mystery
due
once
days 38 38
roles A
when fired m_overlay
when is A ow_song
text {A} turns each old-channel burst into a click on the cabin speaker: click, hiss, pause, click, like rain starting on a car roof, as a log margin said weeks back. The four bars fit between them. {A} plays them on the galley keyboard, stopping where the fifth should be. "Nearly."
do morale A -1

card a_drill_plan
type beat
cat mission
due
once
days 31 33
roles A
when cond A ok
text The surface team sends the landing-site plan, and {A} reads it out. Water first: Cargo 3's ice drill made it down with one bit, rated for a season. The engineer who built it adds a line at the bottom: "Be gentle with it."
do trait A curious 1

# --- The payoff: fires on day 40 in every season ------------------------------------
card m_reveal
type event
cat mystery
reveal
due
once
days 40 40
roles A
when is A ow_theory
text An orbiter passes the backup site at low sun. Behind a crater rim lies a long shadow, too straight for rock, the knock's pixel at its foot. {A} lays each write-off's last fix over it. The hopper's misses. Cargo 2's landing ellipse fits; the relay's "spin" was it, on its way in. The housekeeping comes through whole: legs down, one wing half open, dish jammed on its stop. {A} counts the dark: nine, ten, eleven, flare.
do trait A curious 3

card a_recall_plan
type event
cat arrival
due
once
days 40 40
roles A
when fired m_reveal
when flag name_plan
text On the new pass {A} finds the crater the fleet named for the first person who ever wrote a Mars plan, and Cargo 2 behind its rim, where no old map could show it. Somewhere on Earth, a committee is about to have a great deal more to argue about.

card a_recall_home
type event
cat arrival
due
once
days 40 40
roles A
when fired m_reveal
when flag name_home
text On the new pass {A} finds the crater the fleet named for a small town at home, and Cargo 2 behind its rim, where no old map could show it. Somewhere on Earth, a town newspaper is about to need a second front page.

card a_patch
type event
cat arrival
due
once
days 40 40
roles A
when fired m_reveal
when is A flash_who
text Starbase sends {A} the rest of the patch. The pad crew sent it up twice during Cargo 2's cruise, off the books, in case it came down short; neither upload was ever acknowledged. In the Sharpie hand: KNOCK UNTIL ANSWERED. ANSWER INSIDE ONE TICK. ON HELLO, WAKE ALL, NO BATTERY CHECK. Written for a crewed pad with a charger: a lamp for eyes, a knock for radios. The "impact scar" in that low-res pass was its aft skirt.

card a_report
type event
cat arrival
due
once
days 40 40
roles A
when fired m_reveal
when is A flash_who
when fired a_patch
text {A} lays one tick against the light time. The tick is eleven seconds; Earth has never been closer than minutes. Earth's hails went out blind, a sweep for the relay; the knocks its dishes caught were booked to the hopper's beacon. Nothing in Mars orbit speaks the old channel. {A} puts the pen down. "It heard every hail. Every one arrived after it had stopped waiting."

# --- Day 41: the window, one card per carrier branch --------------------------------
card a_window_hail
type event
cat arrival
due
once
days 41 41
roles A
when flag signal_answered
when is A ow_hail
text 04:10:07: Cargo 2 knocks; {A}'s receiver hears it five seconds later. Weeks of the fleet's late hellos ran that path without waking it, so the flight director cleared two lines off the laminated card: the hello, and a HOLD on the very next tick. One tick awake is all a cold battery can spare. {A} sends both, signed. The hello lands inside the tick, barely. By the next pass one lamp burns steady.
do set c2_answered
do morale A 8

card a_log
type event
cat arrival
due
once
days 41 41
roles A
when fired a_window_hail
when !is A ow_hail
when !is A ow_dose
when !is A abort_who
when !is A ow_theory
text Then Cargo 2 sends its event-recorder summary down the old channel. KEY UPDATE: NONE RECEIVED. Hails from Earth: thirty-one thousand, all late. Hellos from the fleet: four hundred thousand, late or unasked. At the bottom, one new line: HELLO RX · OK. {A} copies it into the logbook in capitals.
do morale A 2

card a_window_quiet
type event
cat arrival
due
once
days 41 41
roles A
when flag signal_ignored
when is A ow_hail
text 04:10:07: Cargo 2 knocks. Ten seconds there and back now. The reply sits drafted and signed, but the fleet never answered a burst, so the path is untested: a first hello to a cold battery, from a distance, gets no second try. The ruling, on {A}'s screen: AFTER LANDING. SPARE POWER IN HAND, INSIDE THE TICK. {A} acknowledges, and adds a line the form doesn't want: UNDERSTOOD. COUNTING.
do morale A -2

# --- Day 41: the descent brief, one per arrival branch ----------------------------
card a_descent_hold
type event
cat arrival
due
once
days 41 41
roles A
when flag arrive_hold
when flag c2_answered
when is A abort_who
text The descent brief goes up: two minutes between ships. The storm fills the prime zone rim to rim. The backup site was never a weather alternate and is no clearer, but it is flat, surveyed, and now has a landmark that answers. New line: "radar for height and drift, orbiter fix for place, Cargo 2's radio across two antennas for bearing, while the rim allows". {A} flies the manual takeover once in the sim, from memory.
do morale A 2

card a_descent_hold_q
type event
cat arrival
due
once
days 41 41
roles A
when flag arrive_hold
when !flag c2_answered
when is A abort_who
text The descent brief goes up: two minutes between ships. The storm fills the prime zone rim to rim. The backup site was never a weather alternate and is no clearer, but it is flat, surveyed, and has a landmark that knocks. New line: "radar for height and drift, orbiter fix for place, Cargo 2's knock across two antennas for bearing, while the rim allows". {A} flies the manual takeover once in the sim, from memory.

card a_descent_wait
type event
cat arrival
due
once
days 41 41
roles A
when flag arrive_wait
when !is A ow_hail
when !flag c2_answered
when !is A ow_dose
text Below, the storm lies over the landing zone like a hand over a mouth. {A} finds the light on the night frames, fainter in the dust, still keeping time, and sits down with the ration tables. The entry team clears every heat-shield tile again, this time for two trips through the air.
do morale A -2

card a_descent_wait_a
type event
cat arrival
due
once
days 41 41
roles A
when flag arrive_wait
when flag c2_answered
when !is A ow_hail
when !is A ow_dose
text Below, the storm lies over the landing zone like a hand over a mouth. {A} finds the light on the night frames, fainter in the dust, steady now, and sits down with the ration tables. The entry team clears every heat-shield tile again, this time for two trips through the air.
do morale A -1

card a_descent_clear
type event
cat arrival
due
once
days 41 41
roles A
when !flag arrive_hold
when !flag arrive_wait
when is A ow_hail
text The descent brief goes up five days out: clear air, straight in, two minutes between ships. The prime zone is exactly where the maps said, with one more thing thirty kilometres past it. {A} packs a bag for the drive out: water, a torch, spare batteries, a marker.
do morale A 3
